###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The paper identifies the models by name, training set and parameter count (Table IV), not by release. They are matched to registry models by parameter count: M3GNet (188k MPF, 228k) to the model of chen2022, MACE-MP-0 (4.69M) to the 2023.12.03 release, CHGNet (413k) to v0.3.0. Worth confirming against the code repository of the paper.
# - SevenNet-0 is 'built upon NequIP' and MatterSim-v1 'builds upon M3GNet' (the paper's words), so their registry stubs apply entity:NequIP and entity:M3GNet; ORB and eqV2-M get their own registry methods.
# - The CHGNet energy MAE of 334 meV/atom is high because the energy correction used in CHGNet training was not applied (stated by the authors).
# - Not encoded for lack of a MetricProperty: volume MAE, failure rates, MAE of the maximum phonon frequency, vibrational entropy, Helmholtz free energy, heat capacity, phonon DOS and sound velocities (Table II), and the dynamical-stability confusion matrix (Table III).
# - No model is trained in this paper, so there is no training data set, sampling strategy or hyperparameter setting; the PBE reference calculation is declared but not attached to a data set.
# - GPU/CPU timings mentioned in the discussion were not captured.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

